// claim: **No termination bound.**
// The claim is an absence, which no program can show by finishing. What runs
// here is the nearest thing that does finish: a loop bounded by nothing but
// its own `@!` goes round as many times as it is told.
n = 0
@ {
    n = n + 1
    ? n >= 200000 { @! }
}
>> n ¶                // → 200000
